        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For 40 years, ever since the decision in Baker versus Carr, State court judges, like Federal judges, have played a role in addressing constitutional problems stemming from malapportionment. This was reflected in Scott versus Germano in 1965, and again in Growe versus Emison in 1993 when the Court said not only that State judges play a role, but they are preferred to Federal judges as agents of reapportionment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, did -- did Mississippi appeal from the injunction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But -- but the issue is whether the State was still pursuing the -- the redistricting that was the subject of the application to the Attorney General, and whether it was doing so or not depended upon whether the State was appealing from the Federal injunction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: But does it remove the Federal obstacle if -- instead of passing on the hypothetical of whether the Federal ground, which is a alternative ground, et cetera is good or bad -- if we just repeated the language from Wise versus Lipscomb, said it's premature to decide this constitutional issue, our cases say not to, but there's an alternative ground here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McDuff",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McDUFF: The -- the 60 days, in our view, Justice Breyer, has already run."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's our position that the State court redistricting plan was not precleared on either of the two occasions that appellants --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0002-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We moved for a stay at the Supreme Court of Mississippi. That stay was denied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Parties",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0002-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "the Supreme Court of Mississippi, according to some of the parties, has overturned previous cases of that court which said the chancery court lacks the power to enter the plan"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But would you say it's absolutely correct if the constitutional reasoning were wrong, and if they say we won't approve a -- a Mississippi plan that is in violation of our constitutional holding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no regulation that allow -- by which the Justice Department says, we will not continue to -- to consider a -- a plan that has been enjoined on constitutional grounds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0003-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba22edaf8247b97c013cabe81480a44e8f3170976523464802586543311e6192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba22edaf8247-0003-0001",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the creation of the situation where Mississippi can conduct its elections in 2004 without continued confusion of the type that we had at the last election"
    }
  ],
